---
layout: layouts/page.njk
title: "Contact | The Café"
description: "Get in touch with The Café in Leavenworth, KS. Phone, email, and location, plus our weekly menu newsletter signup."
ogDescription: "Get in touch with The Café in Leavenworth, KS. Contact info, FAQ, and weekly menu newsletter signup."
pageCss: "/assets/css/contact.css"
---
<section class="section" aria-labelledby="contact-heading">
            <div class="container">

                <!-- ── Heading + catering pointer ───────────── -->
                <h1 id="contact-heading">Contact Us</h1>
                <p style="margin-top: 0.75rem; max-width: 55ch;">
                    Planning an event? Our booking form on the catering page has everything
                    we need to get started on your quote.
                </p>
                <a href="catering#inquiry" class="btn btn-primary" style="margin-top: 1.25rem; display: inline-block;">Book a Catering</a>

                <!-- ── Contact Info ─────────────────────────── -->
                <div class="contact-info">
                    <h2>Get in Touch</h2>
                    <ul class="contact-info__list">
                        <li>Hours: {{ site.opening.hoursDays }}, {{ site.opening.opens.time }}&nbsp;{{ site.opening.opens.meridiem }} &ndash; {{ site.opening.closes.time }}&nbsp;{{ site.opening.closes.meridiem }}</li>
                        <li>Phone: <a href="tel:+19135479994">(913) 547-9994</a></li>
                        <li>Email: <a href="mailto:theabcafe@gmail.com">theabcafe@gmail.com</a></li>
                        <li>Location: <a href="https://maps.google.com/?q=417+S+6th+St,+Leavenworth,+KS+66048">417 S 6th St, Leavenworth, KS 66048</a></li>
                    </ul>
                </div>

                <!-- ── Newsletter Signup ────────────────────── -->
                <div class="contact-info" id="newsletter">
                    <h2>Get Our Weekly Menu &amp; News</h2>
                    <p style="margin-top: 0.75rem; max-width: 55ch;">
                        Be first to hear what's cooking: weekly menus, catering specials, and news
                        from the kitchen, straight to your inbox.
                    </p>

                    <!-- Formspree, which emails each sign-up. Email only since
                         2026-10-09: no phone number or texting, which aren't planned. -->
                    <form action="https://formspree.io/f/mdarqnql" method="POST"
                          data-success="You're on the list! Watch your inbox for weekly menus and news from the kitchen.">
                        <input type="text" name="_gotcha" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off"
                               style="position:absolute; left:-9999px;" aria-hidden="true">
                        <input type="hidden" name="_subject" value="Newsletter signup: website form">

                        <div class="form-grid">
                            <div class="form-group">
                                <label for="nl-email">Email <span style="color:var(--accent-dark)">*</span></label>
                                <input type="email" id="nl-email" name="email" autocomplete="email" required placeholder="you@example.com">
                            </div>


                            <div class="form-group form-group--full">
                                <button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary">Sign Me Up</button>
                                <p class="form-hint" style="margin-top: 0.6rem;">
                                    Unsubscribe anytime. See our <a href="privacy">privacy policy</a>.
                                </p>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </form>
                </div>

                <!-- ── FAQ ─────────────────────────────────── -->
                <div class="faq">
                    <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
                    {#- Answers are the client's own (CafeWork DECISIONS.md §8,
                        2026-09-30). Two old questions came out rather than get
                        invented answers: cancellation policy (not decided) and
                        serving staff (the full-service offer is gone). -#}
                    <ul class="faq__list">
                        <li>
                            <p class="faq__q">How far ahead should I order for a group?</p>
                            <p class="faq__a">For more than 10 people, please give us at least 12 hours&rsquo; notice. Larger custom catering takes a few weeks to plan, so reach out as early as you can.</p>
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            <p class="faq__q">Can I order ahead?</p>
                            {%- if site.phoneOrders %}
                            <p class="faq__a">Yes. Call <a href="tel:{{ site.phoneHref }}">{{ site.phone }}</a> and we&rsquo;ll have it ready for pickup.{% if not site.ordering.url %} Online ordering is coming soon.{% endif %}</p>
                            {%- elif site.ordering.url %}
                            <p class="faq__a">Yes. <a href="{{ site.ordering.url }}">Order online</a> and pick it up at the counter.</p>
                            {%- else %}
                            <p class="faq__a">Not yet. For our first few weeks, please order at the counter. Online ordering is coming soon. Group orders for catering can still be arranged ahead; see <a href="/catering">Catering</a>.</p>
                            {%- endif %}
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            <p class="faq__q">How can I pay?</p>
                            <p class="faq__a">Cash, check, or card.</p>
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            <p class="faq__q">Do you accommodate dietary restrictions?</p>
                            <p class="faq__a">Tell us about any allergies or dietary needs when you order and we&rsquo;ll let you know what we can do.</p>
                        </li>
                    </ul>
                </div>

            </div>
        </section>
